{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-238352-r4515719","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Fried Pickle","sourcePageId":238352,"sourceRevision":"4515719","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T16:22:33Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Fried%20Pickle&oldid=4515719","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:54:20.218Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Deep fried recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using cucumber pickles","Category:Recipes using dill","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using hot sauce","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Southern U.S. recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"57b2d67038eb428e2d60d2515848ced7fea618a4b9c671feacba8ab26676a514","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary\n| category = Snack recipes\n| servings = 8\n| time = 20 minutes\n| difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[File:FRIED PICKLES, HONEY.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|United States]] | [[Cookbook:Snacks|Snacks]]\n\n'''Fried pickle''' is a snack item found in the American South. It is made by deep-frying a sliced, battered, [[w:dill pickle|dill pickle]]. \n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Milk mixture ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]], beaten\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|flour]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* 6 drops [[Cookbook:Hot Sauce|hot sauce]]\n\n=== Flour mixture ===\n* 3½ cup flour\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Tsp|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ¾ tsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n\n=== Other ingredients ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Quart|qt]] [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] dill [[Cookbook:Pickle|pickles]]\n* Dried [[Cookbook:Dill|dill]] (optional)\n* [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|Vegetable oil]] for deep frying\n\n==Procedure==\n#Combine the ingredients for the milk mixture, stirring well. Set aside. \n#Combine ingredients for the flour mixture, stirring well. \n#Dip pickles in milk mixture and [[Cookbook:Dredging|dredge]] in flour mixture. Repeat process. \n#[[Cookbook:Deep Fat Frying|Deep fry]] in oil heated to 350 °F until pickles float to surface and are golden brown. Drain on [[Cookbook:Paper Towel|paper towels]]. \n#Sprinkle with dried dill to your liking.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using cucumber pickles]]\n[[Category:Deep fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with images]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using hot sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dill]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Fried Pickle","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"8","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup milk","sourceText":"1 cup milk","amountText":"1 cup milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 egg, beaten","sourceText":"1 egg, beaten","amountText":"1 egg, beaten","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tbsp flour","sourceText":"1 tbsp flour","amountText":"1 tbsp flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":nul